## Releasing and promoting

CI in each app repo writes `environments/{{ defaults.RELEASE_ENVIRONMENT }}/<workload>/release.yaml` on every
push to main, so `{{ defaults.RELEASE_ENVIRONMENT }}` always runs the latest build. To promote, copy that file to
another environment and merge it:

```sh
cp environments/{{ defaults.RELEASE_ENVIRONMENT }}/api/release.yaml environments/production/api/release.yaml
```

Nothing deploys to an environment until its `release.yaml` exists.

## Run it locally

Needs Docker, [k3d](https://k3d.io), kubectl and Helm:

```sh
./scripts/bootstrap-local.sh
```

This creates a k3d cluster, installs Argo CD (chart {{ defaults.ARGO_CD_CHART_VERSION }}) and applies
`bootstrap/root.yaml`. Push this repo and the app repos first; Argo CD reads them from
`{{ project.git_base_url }}`. For private repositories, give Argo CD read access, e.g.
`argocd repocreds add {{ project.git_base_url }} --username USER --password TOKEN`.
